sentences.l:
And they purified themselves and cast the filth into the salt-sea,
and offered to Apollo complete hecatombs
of bulls and of goats along the shore of the unharvested salt-sea;

for truly he, in baleful wits, rages,
nor does he know at all how to think at once forward and backward,
how for him beside the ships the Achaeans may fight safe.”

So he spoke, and Patroclus obeyed his dear companion,
and out of the hut led Briseis, fair-cheeked,
and gave her to lead away;

but Achilles,
in tears, from his companions at once sat down, withdrawn apart,
on the shore of the grey sea, looking out over the boundless open-sea;

“Mother, since you bore me, short-lived though I am,
honour at least to me ought to have granted the Olympian
Zeus high-thundering;

and him, Apollo,
when he prayed, heard, since very dear to him he was,
and sent upon the Argives an evil shaft;

and those people
were dying, one close upon another, and the shafts of the god went about
everywhere through the wide army of the Achaeans;
